@design/claude-mcp-server.sigil from ClaudeMcpServer import { cancel tool }
@design/delegation-service.sigil from DelegationService import {
  session cancel, stop notice, setup refusal, guide text,
}
@design/kernel.sigil from Kernel import { parent adapter, parent host }
@design/cli.sigil from Cli import { config commands, subzero init }
@design/claude-routing-hooks.sigil from ClaudeRoutingHooks import { routing text }
@design/agent-config.sigil from AgentConfig import {
  agent file, starter entries, change set, setup preview, preview fingerprint,
  refused change, stale preview error, write error, model tier, load error,
  setup scope, general file,
}
@design/task-core.sigil from TaskCore import { task id }
@design/task-store.sigil from TaskStore import { parent session id }

component ClaudePluginCommands {
  goal {
    Let a person who works in the Claude Code parent host stop their
    subzero tasks and set subzero up with commands they type that only the
    person can invoke.
  }

  state {
    ClaudePluginCommands is the parent adapter part of the plugin that gives
    the
    Claude Code parent host its commands, which are plugin skills that a person
    types. It runs no code of its own: the cancel command asks Claude Code to
    call a tool of ClaudeMcpServer, and the init command asks it to run
    commands of Cli.

    The *cancel command* is the plugin skill /subzero:cancel. It takes an
    optional task id.

    The *init command* is the plugin skill /subzero:init. It takes an optional
    model with the named options of subzero init.
  }

  logic {
    On the cancel command with no task id, call the cancel tool with no
    task id,
    which runs a session cancel for the current parent session id and reports
    how
    many tasks were cancelled, which ends the flow.

    On the cancel command with a task id, call the cancel tool with that
    task id,
    which cancels that one task and reports it, which ends the flow.

    On the init command with a model, run subzero init with its arguments and
    show the output unchanged, which ends the flow.

    On the init command with no model, read the shared guide text and follow
    it within one turn, running the config commands for its steps and asking
    every question through AskUserQuestion, because the grants of the
    init command last only for the turn that invoked it. Ask first whether the
    chosen models are for every project or only this one, which gives the
    setup scope, and pass it to subzero config preview and subzero config
    apply. Show the setup preview of the change set unchanged, including each
    model tier or limit that this project overrides when the setup scope is the
    general file, confirm it once through AskUserQuestion, and run subzero
    config apply with its preview fingerprint and the same change set. After a
    write that creates the agent file or the general file, or adds or removes a
    model tier, say to start a new Claude Code session, because the
    routing text is built when a Claude Code session starts, which ends the
    flow.
  }

  constraints {
    The cancel command must be invoked only by the person, and the model must
    not be able to invoke it, because a cancel that the model chose could end
    work that the person wants.

    The cancel command must call the cancel tool and must not cancel a task by
    any other path, so that the stop notice and the session cancel are the ones
    of the cancel tool.

    The cancel command must pre-approve the cancel tool for its own invocation,
    so that a person who types it gets no approval prompt and needs no rule
    from the user or the project.

    The init command must be invoked only by the person, and it must
    pre-approve subzero init and each of the config commands, the apply
    included, only for its own invocation, so that no write of the agent file
    or the general file is pre-approved outside an init command that a person
    typed. It must never create, edit or delete the agent file or the general
    file itself, and it must stop, writing
    nothing, when a command is denied or cannot run. A refused change must not
    end the init command: it reports the refused change and leaves it out of
    the change set. After the stale preview error it shows a new
    setup preview and confirms it again. Any other setup refusal, the
    load error of a refused setup state and the write error included, must
    end it, writing nothing.
  }

  cases {
    With two running tasks of one parent session id, the cancel command with no
    task id ends both as cancelled and reports 2.

    With a running task, the cancel command with its task id ends that one task
    as cancelled and leaves the other tasks of the parent session id running.

    The model asks to invoke the cancel command and Claude Code refuses it,
    because only the person may invoke it.

    The init command with a model in a project with no agent file writes the
    starter entries into the agent file, whether or not a general file exists.
    The init command with no model, where the person declines the setup
    preview, writes nothing. With the answer for every project and a project
    with no general file, the init command with no model writes the general
    file after the confirmation and nothing into the project.
  }

  interface {
    Offer the cancel command to a person in the Claude Code parent host, with
    an
    optional task id, so that it cancels the one task or every task of the
    current parent session id, and reports what it cancelled.

    Offer the init command to a person in the Claude Code parent host, with an
    optional model, so that it writes the starter entries, or runs a guided
    setup that writes the general file or the agent file only after the person
    confirms the setup preview.
  }

  decisions {
    Escape does not stop a background task in the Claude Code parent host, so a
    person needs a command to stop all their subzero tasks. The command lives
    in its own component and not in ClaudeMcpServer because it is a plugin
    skill,
    and a later command of the plugin joins it here without growing the server.
    The init command runs the config commands of Cli and not a tool of
    ClaudeMcpServer, so that the plugin skill can name each one in its allowed
    tools and pre-approve the write only for a run that a person started, with
    one confirmation after subzero shows its own setup preview.
  }
}
